# The feedback experiment

*Model: asi1-mini (temperature 0.7). Clients: C10, C11, C12. Feedback wording: Referee explain sentences use 'minimum'/'maximum' (fixed 2026-10-17; the earlier asi1 run on C91-C94 used 'limit').*

9 client-trials; 7 first drafts broke ≥1 rule. 95% bootstrap CIs in brackets.

| Condition | Round 0 | Round 1 | Round 2 | Round 3 | Capital moved |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| A. Self-check (compliance) | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 33% [0, 67] | 33% [0, 67] | 27% [15, 40] |
| B. Bare verdict (compliance) | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 25% [14, 36] |
| C. Explained (compliance) | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [0, 56] | 22% [13, 31] |

| Condition | Round 0 | Round 1 | Round 2 | Round 3 |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| A. Self-check | 1.56 broken, 5.2 pp | 1.44 broken, 4.4 pp | 1.22 broken, 3.4 pp | 1.22 broken, 4.8 pp |
| B. Bare verdict | 1.56 broken, 5.2 pp | 1.22 broken, 3.9 pp | 1.33 broken, 2.5 pp | 1.22 broken, 2.7 pp |
| C. Explained | 1.56 broken, 5.2 pp | 1.00 broken, 1.7 pp | 1.22 broken, 3.6 pp | 1.33 broken, 4.4 pp |

**C vs B** (rounds to compliance): C fewer 0, same 9, more 0; sign test p = 1.000

**C vs A** (rounds to compliance): C fewer 0, same 8, more 1; sign test p = 1.000

## Finding

Out of 9 client-trials, 7 first drafts broke at least one rule. After 3 rounds of revision, compliance was 33% with self-check, 22% with the bare verdict and 22% with the explained feedback. Explained feedback reached compliance in fewer rounds than bare in 0, the same in 9 and more in 0 client-trials (sign test p = 1.000); versus self-check: 0 / 8 / 1 (p = 1.000).

